\section*{Planar Log-Brunn–Minkowski After Translation}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 091; 2026-09-23), the asserted result is that symmetric convex bodies satisfy logarithmic Brunn--Minkowski in all dimensions, with the stated $L_p$, even-measure, and dilation consequences.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Manuscript 1.}
For a full-dimensional origin-symmetric convex body $K\subset\mathbb R^n$, write $h_K(u)=\sup_{x\in K}x\cdot u$, and for a positive function $g$ on the unit sphere define $W[g]=\{x:x\cdot u\le g(u)\text{ for every unit }u\}$. For every integer $n\ge1$, every such pair $K,L$, and every $\lambda\in[0,1]$, the claim is
\[
 |W[h_K^{1-\lambda}h_L^{\lambda}]|\ge |K|^{1-\lambda}|L|^{\lambda}.
\]
Its stated consequence, for every $0<p<1$, is
\[
 \left|W[((1-\lambda)h_K^p+\lambda h_L^p)^{1/p}]\right|^{p/n}
 \ge(1-\lambda)|K|^{p/n}+\lambda|L|^{p/n}.
\]
Volumes are Lebesgue volumes, and central symmetry is an assumption in both assertions.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 091; 2026-09-23), symmetric polytopes are approximated by smooth even-power weights. Logarithmic concavity of their integrals follows from a variance estimate in moment coordinates, and limits first remove the power smoothing and then the Gaussian regularization.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The logarithmic volume theorem requires origin symmetry. General planar bodies need not become centrally symmetric after a translation, so the nonsymmetric translation clause remains outside its hypotheses.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For manuscript 1 (family 091; 2026-09-23), OpenAI lists Lean statements for this assertion: symmetric convex bodies satisfy logarithmic Brunn--Minkowski in all dimensions, with the stated $L_p$, even-measure, and dilation consequences.

This coverage does not establish a formal proof of the complete problem as stated here.

The linked family Comparator checks are \texttt{LogBrunnMinkowski.lean}.

Their named declarations include \texttt{OAI.LogBrunnMinkowski.main}.

This site has not executed the Lean code. Described statement coverage is not an independent proof check.

\subsection{Status caveat}
The manuscripts were produced by an internal OpenAI model. OpenAI cautions that results without formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently checked the proofs; the label records the scope of OpenAI's claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{The logarithmic Brunn–Minkowski conjecture}, 2026-09-23; citation key \texttt{OAI:The-logarithmic-Brunn-Minkowski-conjecture-September-23-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-logarithmic-Brunn-Minkowski-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-logarithmic-Brunn-Minkowski-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-logarithmic-Brunn-Minkowski-conjecture-September-23-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/The-logarithmic-Brunn-Minkowski-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}; Statement source: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-logarithmic-Brunn-Minkowski-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/introduction.tex\#L21}{thm:main, eq:main}.
\item Family 091: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/docs/091.md}{Lean scope}.
\item \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/ComparatorChallenges/LogBrunnMinkowski.json}{Comparator LogBrunnMinkowski.json}.
